    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">First unprovoked seizure (R56.9)</content>. No recurrence in two months without medicine. Most recurrences happen in the first two years, so the safety plan continues. [S]<list><item>No driving until at least six months without a seizure, then a review of how the Hong Kong licence rules apply to him.</item><item>Sparring and full training are fine; falls and work at heights still with a stunt double until six months.</item><item>Epilepsy clinic review at six months, or at once with any event.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic low back pain (M54.50)</content>. Well controlled after the flare; pain 2 out of 10. [S]<list><item>Continue the home program; warm up before every lift; acetaminophen when needed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure recurrence, auras, staring spells and jerks on waking (event diary)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No events in two months</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Neurological examination</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatine kinase and creatinine after a convulsive seizure with exertion</td><td>Until normal (about one week, then as needed)</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Normal at one month; no new event</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium, glucose, calcium and magnesium</td><td>At the event; repeat if abnormal or with a new event</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Normal at the event and at one month</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antiseizure medicine decision</td><td>After the evaluation, and again with any new seizure</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No medicine; he and the clinic reviewed the decision and it stands</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medicines that lower the seizure threshold or cause withdrawal seizures</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Naproxen course finished without side effects; acetaminophen only</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Triggers: sleep, meals, heat, fluids and electrolytes, alcohol and cannabis</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sleep, meals, heat and fluids on plan; no cannabis</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving and dangerous activities</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving; heights paused until six months</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure first aid and safety at work</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood screen</td><td>After a first seizure and yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-2 0 at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Back pain score (0 to 10) and function</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Back pain 2 out of 10 with full training</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Back examination and red flags (saddle sensation, bladder and bowel, leg strength)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No red flags</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise therapy for chronic low back pain</td><td>Ongoing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Home program after the physical therapy course</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Epilepsy clinic review</td><td>Six months after a first seizure, or with any event</td><td>Due</td><td>Booked at six months</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>No further seizures. Outcome by 2026-07-13: None in the two months since the first [S]</item><item>Sleep at least seven hours a night, including on film schedules. Outcome by 2026-06-15: About seven hours a night from the first month [S]</item><item>No cannabis while the seizure risk is highest. Outcome by 2026-07-13: None since the seizure, by his report [S]</item><item>Back pain at 3 or less out of 10 with full training. Outcome by 2026-07-13: Pain 2 out of 10 after a flare that settled within a week [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults: Report of the Guideline Development Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology and the American Epilepsy Society (2015); Practice Parameter: evaluating an apparent unprovoked first seizure in adults (an evidence-based review) (2007); Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017); Supplementary Health Information Sheet for Driver Assessment (First Schedule of the Road Traffic (Driving Licences) Regulations, Cap. 374B) (2021); Neurological disorders: assessing fitness to drive (first unprovoked epileptic seizure) (2026); First Aid for Seizures (2024); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis B vaccine dose 2 in two weeks. Epilepsy clinic and primary care review at six months. Call at once for any event. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
